00:24:19.840 --> 00:24:23.450
<v Jason Kessler>No, that's absolutely not! And you're trying to cuck and save your own ass!
<v Jason Kessler>不，绝对不是！你是在试图通过把责任推给我来保全你自己！

00:24:23.450 --> 00:24:29.260
<v Gavin Mcinnes>No, I'm not! When the mayor said no permit, you knew a fight was going to go down!
<v Gavin Mcinnes>不，我不是！当市长说没有许可证时，你就知道会发生冲突！

00:24:29.260 --> 00:24:40.810
<v Jason Kessler>You cuck yourself for people to save your marriage or your reputation, whatever. And it's just not right, man. You brought me up here to be a patsy for you, just like the Charlottesville government.
<v Jason Kessler>你为了保住你的婚姻或名声之类的东西把自己当成了替罪羊。这根本不对，伙计。你把我带到这里来做你的替罪羊，就像夏洛茨维尔政府一样。

00:24:40.810 --> 00:24:43.930
<v Gavin Mcinnes>Oh, I'm saying the exact opposite. I'm suspicious of you--
<v Gavin Mcinnes>哦，我说的恰恰相反。我很怀疑你——

00:24:43.930 --> 00:25:01.180
<v Zoe Chace>Gavin accepts absolutely no responsibility for some of the guys in his group turning alt-right or white supremacist-esque. Even Sal from the beginning of this story, that Long Island Proud Boy I met at the bar, he went to Charlottesville. He took a selfie with David Duke and tweeted it. He's out of the group now.
<v Zoe Chace>加文对他的组织中有些人变成“另类右翼”或白人至上主义倾向不负任何责任。即使是故事开始时的萨尔，我在酒吧遇到的那个长岛“骄傲男孩”，他也去了夏洛茨维尔。他和戴维·杜克（David Duke）自拍并把它发到了推特上。他现在已经离开了组织。

00:25:01.180 --> 00:25:32.640
<v Gavin Mcinnes>The Proud Boys have zero culpability, not just with his drift right but with the far right in general. And I would argue, if you're looking for someone to blame, that's the leftist media constantly crapping on these young men and telling them that they're evil and that they suck, and I think that the liberal media banding around the word "Nazi" to where it means 50% of the population, is making a lot of young men revolt and go, "Yeah, you know what? I am. How's that, bitch?" I'm not talking to you, calling you a bitch, by the way.
<v Gavin Mcinnes>“骄傲男孩”零责任，不仅是他向右漂移，而且是对极右翼整体。我想说，如果你在找人责备，那就是左翼媒体不断地在这些年轻人身上拉屎，告诉他们他们是邪恶的，他们很烂，我认为自由派媒体围绕“纳粹”这个词，把它定义为50%的人口，正在让许多年轻人反抗并说，“是的，你知道吗？我是。那又怎样，婊子？”顺便说一句，我不是在对你说话，叫你婊子。

00:25:32.640 --> 00:25:34.060
<v Zoe Chace>I know.
<v Zoe Chace>我知道。

00:25:34.060 --> 00:25:42.010
<v Ira Glass>Fact is, there's overlap between what the Proud Boys espouse and what white supremacist groups believe. I ran through the list for Gavin.
<v Ira Glass>事实是，“骄傲男孩”所拥护的与白人至上主义团体所相信的之间有重叠。我为加文列举了清单。

00:25:42.010 --> 00:25:59.920
<v Zoe Chace>"Our culture is better than yours. Our women need to stay home and make more babies. Our country has no more space for immigrants. We are being persecuted." Those are your ideas. Those are ideas I see in white supremacist groups. Do you see that you guys have those same ideas?
<v Zoe Chace>“我们的文化比你们的好。我们的女人需要呆在家里生更多的孩子。我们的国家没有空间容纳移民了。我们正在受到迫害。”这些是你的想法。这些是我在白人至上主义团体中看到的想法。你看到你们有这些相同的想法了吗？

00:25:59.920 --> 00:26:32.470
<v Gavin Mcinnes>Yes, I do. And that's the plight of the right in many ways. This is why William F Buckley had to struggle hard to get Nazis out of National Review. They get attracted to this. But to sort of glom on all this pattern and try to suck everyone into Charlottesville, including the president, is insane. It's an obsession. It's a compulsion. You're falling into the logical fallacy of all cats are mammals, all dogs are mammals, all cats are dogs.
<v Gavin Mcinnes>是的，我看到了。这是右翼在许多方面的困境。这就是为什么小威廉·F·巴克利（William F Buckley）不得不努力将纳粹赶出《国家评论》（National Review）。他们被这个吸引。但要把所有这些模式联系起来，并试图把每个人都拉进夏洛茨维尔，包括总统，是疯狂的。这是一种痴迷。这是一种强迫症。你陷入了所有的猫都是哺乳动物，所有的狗都是哺乳动物，所有的猫都是狗的逻辑谬误中。

00:26:32.470 --> 00:26:41.440
<v Zoe Chace>I think what I've documented is that when you have a group that is founded in part around male resentment and aggrievement without racism--
<v Zoe Chace>我认为我记录下来的是，当你有一个部分建立在男性不满和委屈之上而没有种族主义的团体时——

