<v Gavin Mcinnes>It's not founded around male resentment.
<v Gavin Mcinnes>它不是建立在男性不满之上的。

00:26:43.420 --> 00:26:47.330
<v Zoe Chace>Some people are skipping the "without racism" part. And that's what I'm seeing.
<v Zoe Chace>有些人跳过了“没有种族主义”的部分。而那正是，我看到的。

00:26:47.330 --> 00:27:19.240
<v Gavin Mcinnes>I know that's your thesis. And I'm telling you you're totally and utterly wrong. I'm telling you, Zoe, your entire angle is wrong. Because you found some similarities, because you want to link this to Charlottesville. There was no Proud Boys contingent at that thing. I'm afraid there's no angle here. And the angle of the Proud Boys is not resentment. It's not this animosity. It's just another men's club!
<v Gavin Mcinnes>我知道那是你的论点。我告诉你你完全彻底错了。我告诉你，佐伊，你的整个角度都错了。因为你发现了一些相似之处，因为你想把这个联系到夏洛茨维尔。那件事上没有“骄傲男孩”的人。恐怕这里没有角度。而“骄傲男孩”的角度不是不满。不是这种敌意。这只是另一个男人的俱乐部！

00:27:19.240 --> 00:27:31.560
<v Zoe Chace>Dante didn't know that the guy who organized the Charlottesville rally had been a member of the Proud Boys, and that he'd gone on Gavin's show promoting it. I was the one who told him that during our interview. He had a hard time with it.
<v Zoe Chace>但丁不知道夏洛茨维尔集会的组织者曾是“骄傲男孩”的成员，也不知道他上了加文的节目推广它。在我们的采访中，是我告诉他的。他对此感到很难受。

00:27:31.560 --> 00:28:05.900
<v Dante Nero>That makes my stomach kind of queasy. Really. Like, man. Well, the first thing I'm thinking about is, I gotta get a cover-up for this tattoo. That's got to happen immediately.
<v Dante Nero>这让我的胃有点恶心。真的。像，伙计。好吧，我想到的第一件事是，我必须给这个纹身找个遮盖。这必须立即发生。

00:28:05.900 --> 00:28:20.170
<v Zoe Chace>Just because there's a Jason Kessler or there's a Sal, like, does that mean that there's a slippery slope with all these Proud Boys gonna tumble down it?
