<v Zoe Chace>Well, what is it about that group that created that slippery slope?
<v Zoe Chace>那么，那个团体里有什么东西造成了那个滑坡？

00:28:38.650 --> 00:29:01.200
<v Dante Nero>The perception of being disenfranchised. Not even the reality of it. The fact that you can't just do-- just being a mediocre white dude gets you certain things.
<v Dante Nero>被剥夺权利的感觉。甚至不是那种现实。仅仅是做一个平庸的白人伙计就能让你得到某些东西这一事实。

00:29:01.200 --> 00:29:26.170
<v Zoe Chace>I did talk to guys who were in it for the beer and the friendship and the no-wank solidarity, but also obviously, guys who were in it for "the West is the best." And as Dante says, that's not such a big jump over to "white people are the best." Which really upsets him. He told me this story, that the very first time Dante had Gavin on his podcast, like back two years ago now, they sat down, he and Gavin, and started talking about politics.
<v Zoe Chace>我确实和那些为了啤酒和友谊以及“不手淫”团结在一起的人交谈过，但显然，也和那些为了“西方是最好的”在一起的人交谈过。正如但丁所说，那离“白人是最好的”并没有太大的跨度。这真的让他很困扰。他告诉我这个故事，就在但丁第一次在播客上邀请加文时，比如两年前，他和加文坐下来，开始谈论政治。

00:29:26.170 --> 00:30:01.260
<v Dante Nero>I said, "you know what's interesting is how confident you are about your ideas." And I go, "in general, white dudes that have these ideas, you're so confident about this, but you've never been right on the ethical side of history ever, in the course of history. Coming here and taking the land from the Indians and genocide of Indians, when you talk about the Atlantic slave trade, then when you talk about the intern-- Japanese internment camps. You have Jim Crow. Then you have the mass incarceration. You have police brutality."
<v Dante Nero>我说，“你知道有趣的是你对你的想法有多自信。”我走，“总的来说，有这些想法的白人伙计，你们对此如此自信，但你们在历史进程中，在道德层面从来没有对过。来到这里从印第安人手中夺取土地和印第安人种族灭绝，当你谈论大西洋奴隶贸易时，然后当你谈论日本拘留营时。你们有吉姆·克劳法。然后你们有大规模监禁。你们有警察暴行。”

00:30:01.260 --> 00:30:40.470
<v Dante Nero>And I go, "every time you come up with one of these ideas, you always think you're right, but you're wrong every time in history." I go, "just like this Muslim ban thing that you guys, or deporting the Mexicans, you're sure about this. But you are never right. Never in history have you been right. And history has always shown that because of your lack of-- your insensitivity, your lack of empathy, you don't see it from the oppressed position. You think you're right, and you have the confidence of somebody who is always right when you're always wrong, just never been right."
<v Dante Nero>我走，“每次你们提出这些想法之一时，你们总是认为你们是对的，但你们在历史上每次都错了。”我走，“就像你们这些家伙的穆斯林禁令，或者驱逐墨西哥人，你们对此很确定。但你们从来没有对过。在历史上你们从来没有对过。历史总是表明，由于你们缺乏——你们的麻木不仁，你们缺乏同理心，你们没有从被压迫的位置来看待它。你们认为你们是对的，你们拥有总是正确的人的自信，而在你们总是错的时候，只是从来没有正确过。”

00:30:40.470 --> 00:30:48.870
<v Dante Nero>And he kind of was like, "yeah, that's a good point." After that, we never really talked about politics.
<v Dante Nero>他有点像，“是的，那是一个好的观点。”在那之后，我们就没怎么谈论政治了。

00:30:48.870 --> 00:31:19.590
<v Zoe Chace>This is basically the opposite of "the West is the best," obviously. Dante is definitely upset about Charlottesville. He's upset someone died. He's upset about Nazis. But in the mix of what's frustrating Dante right now is, he feels like the guys misunderstood no-wanks. And the thing they misunderstood about no-wanks is the same thing he thinks they misunderstand about history. They leave out the empathy. No-wanks, as Dante saw it, was supposed to lead to a friendlier, more understanding, and more inclusive world. Or kinda.
<v Zoe Chace>显然，这基本上是“西方是最好的”的对立面。但丁对夏洛茨维尔肯定感到不安。他对有人死了感到不安。他对纳粹感到不安。但在但丁现在感到沮丧的事情中，他觉得这些人误解了“不手淫”。而他们对“不手淫”误解的东西，和他认为他们对历史误解的东西是一样的。他们丢掉了同理心。正如但丁所看到的，“不手淫”本来是为了带来一个更友好、更理解、更具包容性的世界。或者某种程度上。

00:31:19.590 --> 00:31:47.470
<v Dante Nero>I would say "empathy." I would talk about empathy. I started to talk about empathy, understanding the need to see, see it from a woman's perspective. Because how do you-- how do you-- how do you get a woman and have a real intimate relationship if you don't have empathy for what she's going through? Look, I think the anti-pc culture is-- I think that that's a reasonable thing. I think it has gone nuts. I mean, I'm a comic. I want to be able to say what I want to say.
<v Dante Nero>我会说“同理心”。我会谈论同理心。我开始谈论同理心，理解从女性角度来看的需要。因为你怎么——你怎么——如果你对她正在经历的事情没有同理心，你怎么能得到一个女人并拥有一段真正的亲密关系呢？看，我认为反PC文化是——我认为那是合理的事情。我认为它已经疯了。我的意思是，我是个喜剧演员。我想要能够说出我想说的话。

00:31:47.470 --> 00:31:48.150
